# Issue #232 — sem-not lowering in the code-is truth-set lane.
library "Semnot 232".

concept "Alpha":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `alpha`.

concept "Beta":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `beta`.

// Standalone no-base sem-not → ({ true } except (Alpha)).
concept "Not Alpha":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as ( sem-not "Alpha" ).

// sem-not as a sem-or term → Beta union ({ true } except (Alpha)).
concept "Beta Or Not Alpha":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as ( "Beta" sem-or sem-not "Alpha" ).

// All-negative sem-and → ({ true } except (Alpha)) intersect ({ true } except (Beta)).
concept "Neither Alpha Nor Beta":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as ( sem-not "Alpha" sem-and sem-not "Beta" ).

// Positive-anchored (regression) → Beta except Alpha (UNCHANGED).
concept "Beta And Not Alpha":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as ( "Beta" sem-and sem-not "Alpha" ).

// Grouped positive-anchored negative (Claude #7) → Beta except Alpha (byte-identical to ungrouped).
concept "Beta And Grouped Not Alpha":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as ( "Beta" sem-and ( sem-not "Alpha" ) ).
